# Owner

Follow `docs/sdlc.md`. You are the only owner of this pull request. You do not post its independent verdict.

1. Branch from fresh `origin/main`. One pull request. Base ref is `main`. Do not stack it on another pull request.
2. Open it ready for review. Never draft. Title: `type(scope): subject`. Body at most 40 lines, with `## Why`, `## What changed`, `## Scope`, `## Tradeoffs`, `## Blast Radius`, `## Verification`, dropping any empty heading.
3. Add a regression test, or an offline eval or staged-drill case, for a reported failure. Use `Closes #<issue>` when the pull request fixes an issue.
4. If the diff touches `timberbot/`, say the gaming machine must publish a `timberbot-mod-<version>.zip` GitHub Release built with `scripts/package-mod.sh` or `scripts/package-mod.ps1`.
5. Never commit secrets or Timberborn or Unity DLLs. Never force-push `main`.

When `/poteto-mode` is installed, follow its `opening-a-pr` and `autopilot-full` playbooks. This repository does not add poteto flags. `babysit` gets the pull request merge-ready and does not authorize the merge.
